/* The Windows resource block for tadpole.exe and tadpole-view.exe.
 *
 * ICON ID 1, AND THE NUMBER MATTERS. Explorer, the taskbar and Alt-Tab all
 * show the icon with the LOWEST numeric ID, not the first one declared.
 *
 * THE DESKTOP SHORTCUT INHERITS THIS, which is the whole point. The installer
 * creates it as
 *
 *   CreateShortCut "$DESKTOP\...lnk" "$INSTDIR\tadpole.exe" "" "$INSTDIR\tadpole.exe" 0
 *
 * — icon index 0 of tadpole.exe itself — so there is no separate .ico to
 * install, nothing to go stale, and a shortcut the user makes by hand gets the
 * same artwork as the one the installer made.
 *
 * IT IS THE GLASSPOLE LOGO ON A FILE CALLED tadpole.exe, and that is
 * deliberate: on Windows the product IS Glasspole, the viewer already rebrands
 * itself at runtime, and the executable names are internal plumbing nobody
 * chose to look at. Matching the window would be worse than matching the name.
 *
 * The icon lives at the repository root and is shared with glasspole.exe.
 * Regenerate from glasspole.png with tools/make-icon.py. */
1 ICON "../../glasspole.ico"
